Phase 2: license SPI + extract EncryptionService behind engine-spi interface

engine-spi (new):
- ai.myrmec.engine.spi.license: LicenseService, LicenseFeature (7 starter
  features), LicenseTier (COMMUNITY/ENTERPRISE/ENTERPRISE_PLUS), LicenseState
  (PENDING/ACTIVE/GRACE/EXPIRED/REVOKED), LicenseSnapshot, LicenseEntry,
  @ConditionalOnLicense annotation + LicenseCondition (REGISTER_BEAN phase).
- ai.myrmec.engine.spi.crypto.EncryptionService: encrypt/decrypt SPI.

engine-core:
- CommunityLicenseService (always reports COMMUNITY tier, denies all features)
  registered by LicenseAutoConfiguration with @ConditionalOnMissingBean.
- Existing _system.crypto.EncryptionService renamed to BasicEncryptionService
  (git mv, history preserved), now implements the SPI; registered by
  CryptoAutoConfiguration with @ConditionalOnMissingBean.
- META-INF/spring/org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.AutoConfiguration.imports
  added so both auto-configs load on classpath scan.
- 5 callers switched from the concrete _system.crypto.EncryptionService to
  the spi.crypto.EncryptionService interface (ModelService,
  LocalSecretBackendAdapter, AuthProviderService, UserAuthService,
  IntegrationTestBase).

Tests (38 green):
- 4 new LicenseServiceWithoutEnterpriseTest cases verify Community bean wins,
  tier=COMMUNITY, all features denied, snapshot empty, encryption round-trip.
- All 24 pre-existing unit tests + 10 AddressBookScenarioIT tests still pass.

Proves the SPI machinery: an Enterprise jar can now replace either bean by
publishing its own ahead of these auto-configs without touching any caller.
